#!/bin/sh
# prodsql "<SQL>"  ->  SELECT en 140, sesion de SOLO LECTURA. La contrasena no viaja
# por la linea de comandos: sale del coinalyze.env del propio 140, dentro de 140.
set -eu
B=/srv/coinanalyze/harness; . "$B/env"
q="$*"
[ -n "$q" ] || { echo 'uso: prodsql "SELECT ..."' >&2; exit 2; }
case "$q" in
  *[Ss][Ee][Ll][Ee][Cc][Tt]*) ;;
  *) echo "prodsql solo acepta consultas. Para escribir esta el espejo." >&2; exit 3 ;;
esac
enc=$(printf '%s' "$q" | base64 | tr -d '\n')
payload=$(cat <<PAYLOAD
if [ -r /etc/coinalyze/coinalyze.env ]; then set -a; . /etc/coinalyze/coinalyze.env; set +a; fi
export PGHOST=\${PG_HOST:-127.0.0.1} PGPORT=\${PG_PORT:-5432}
export PGUSER=${PROD_PG_USER} PGDATABASE=${PROD_PG_DB}
[ -n "\${PG_PASSWORD:-}" ] && export PGPASSWORD="\$PG_PASSWORD"
export PGOPTIONS='-c default_transaction_read_only=on -c statement_timeout=60000'
printf %s '$enc' | base64 -d | psql -X -A -F'|' -t -v ON_ERROR_STOP=1 -q -f -
PAYLOAD
)
penc=$(printf '%s' "$payload" | base64 | tr -d '\n')
ssh -n -o BatchMode=yes -o ConnectTimeout=8 \
  -i "$PROD_SSH_KEY" -o UserKnownHostsFile="$PROD_KNOWN_HOSTS" \
  "$PROD_SSH_USER@$PROD_HOST" "printf %s $penc | base64 -d | sh" 2>&1 | "$B/bin/_corta"
